  "summary": "A pleated black-wool bell skirt UNESCO calls an endangered masterpiece of Albanian dress.",
  "description": "The xhubleta is the wildest silhouette in European dress: a heavy wool skirt hung from shoulder straps that flares into a dozen or more roped cord-pleats, so stiff it rings like a bell as the wearer walks. Woven on narrow looms in black with white zigzag and moon symbols that signal region, clan and life stage, it takes months to make and belonged to the women of Malësia's mountain clans, the land of the Kanun codes. Production nearly died under communist collectivization; UNESCO inscribed it as intangible heritage in urgent need of safeguarding, and highland ateliers now re-taught the pleating to a new generation.",
  "culturalContext": "Within Malësia's mountain clan society (the customary Kanun legal sphere), the xhubleta marked womanhood, region and life stage; its near-extinction under communist collectivization and UNESCO's 2022 urgent-safeguarding listing turned it into a national symbol of Albanian highland identity and a living women's craft economy.",
